---
import CaseLayout from '../../layouts/CaseLayout.astro';
import Img from '../../components/Img.astro';
import Video from '../../components/Video.astro';
import Steps from '../../components/Steps.astro';
---
<CaseLayout
  slug="releaf"
  eyebrow="Startup · Founder"
  title="ReLeaf Candles"
  summary="Candles that have a second life. Burn it, twist the base open, and your candle becomes a planter."
  hero="/images/releaf/hero.webp"
  heroAlt="The Canduela candle on a wood slice beside the same jar turned into a lavender planter"
  snapshot={[
    ['My role', 'Founder + CEO'],
    ['Started', 'High school Virtual Enterprise'],
    ['Milestones', 'SVC finalist, IdeaBounce win'],
    ['Next', 'Pilot program in California'],
  ]}
>
  <section id="problem" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="The problem">The problem</h2>
    <p>
      My entrepreneurial spark lit up in high school, when I joined Virtual Enterprise, a class that runs a business
      from start to finish. I became CEO, and my team dug into the problem of mass consumption.
    </p>
    <p>
      It blew my mind to learn that <strong>millions of empty candle jars end up in landfills every year</strong>. As a
      candle fanatic, I saw it firsthand. Those gorgeous jars pile up, and most people toss them or let them gather dust.
      Some eco-conscious people turn them into planters, but drilling holes and figuring out drainage is more hassle
      than it’s worth.
    </p>
    <p class="quote">What if candle jars could have a second life?</p>
  </section>

  <section id="how" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="How it works">How it works</h2>
    <p>ReLeaf kits come with everything you need to grow something once your candle is done burning.</p>
    <Steps steps={[
      { label: 'Light it', text: 'Enjoy your candle like any other.' },
      { label: 'Twist it', text: 'Clean the jar and twist the bottom to reveal drainage holes and a hidden seed compartment.' },
      { label: 'Grow it', text: 'Add the provided soil and click the lid onto the base as a water plate. Or bury the whole thing: it biodegrades in a few months.' },
    ]} />
    <figure class="figure wide">
      <Img src="/images/releaf/how-it-works.webp" alt="Illustrated three-step guide: light the candle, twist the bottom to reveal seeds, add soil and watch it grow" />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="product" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="Product line">The product line</h2>
    <p>
      My love for fragrance shows up here. We started with classic aromatherapy scents: <strong>rosemary, spearmint,
      eucalyptus, and lavender</strong>, plus calendula. Later I want to experiment with seasonal blends.
    </p>
    <figure class="figure wide">
      <Img src="/images/releaf/lineup.webp" alt="Four ReLeaf candles, Spearmint, Rosemary, Calendula and Lavender, on a white podium with mailer boxes" />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="prototypes" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="Prototypes">From idea to prototype</h2>
    <p>
      Fine-tuning the first candle kit MVP was no walk in the park. Some days nothing worked, and doubt showed up
      weekly. But failure kept turning into progress. I learned about manufacturing, the patent process, and how useful
      Excel is for financial projections. A big moment was finding a <strong>biodegradable, heat-resistant material</strong> for the jars.
    </p>
    <Steps steps={[
      { label: 'Idea', text: '3D models of jar, lid, and twist-base variations.', src: '/images/releaf/cad.webp', alt: '3D CAD models of several jar, lid and base variations with annotations' },
      { label: 'First print', text: 'Early clay-toned prototypes, tested with soil.', src: '/images/releaf/first-print.webp', alt: 'Early clay-toned prototype jars, one planted, at a booth' },
      { label: 'Refined', text: 'The Canduela candle, and the same jar as a planter.', src: '/images/releaf/hero.webp', alt: 'Refined Canduela candle and lavender planter' },
    ]} />
  </section>

  <section id="brand" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="Brand identity">Brand identity</h2>
    <p>
      The mark is a single line that reads as both a flame and a sprouting leaf, the whole product story in one shape.
      The palette pulls from parchment, sage, and soil. Tagline: <strong>“Light your peace, plant your joy.”</strong>
    </p>
    <div class="grid-2 wide">
      <figure class="figure"><Img src="/images/releaf/logo.webp" alt="ReLeaf Candles primary logo: Candles That Have a Second Life" /></figure>
      <figure class="figure"><Img src="/images/releaf/brand-guide.webp" alt="Brand guide: signature and pictorial logos, six-color palette, RoxboroughCF and Belleza fonts" /></figure>
    </div>
    <ul class="palette" aria-label="Brand palette">
      {['#f1ead8', '#d5c7ad', '#bec5a4', '#8a8e75', '#68604c', '#2d2f22'].map((c) => <li style={`--sw:${c}`}><span>{c}</span></li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="packaging" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="Packaging">Packaging</h2>
    <p>The mailer box tells the candle-to-plant story before you even open it, with socials on the side.</p>
    <figure class="figure wide">
      <Img src="/images/releaf/packaging.webp" alt="Packaging mockups: a mailer box with a candle-to-plant cycle graphic and a lid card reading Light your peace, plant your joy" />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="social" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="Social">Social media</h2>
    <p>I ran ReLeaf’s Instagram and TikTok: the launch post, trade show stories, and a mission series.</p>
    <figure class="figure wide">
      <Img src="/images/releaf/social.webp" alt="Three phones: a mini tradeshow story collage, the @releafcandles Instagram profile, and the launch post" />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="traction" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="Traction">Trade shows + traction</h2>
    <p>
      The most rewarding part was hearing people’s reactions. At mock trade shows, people told us they’d buy the kit in
      a heartbeat. Networking became one of my favorite parts of the journey. After every competition and pitch, I left
      knowing more and more excited for what’s next.
    </p>
    <div class="grid-2 wide">
      <figure class="figure"><Img src="/images/releaf/tradeshow.webp" alt="The ReLeaf team in green polos at their trade show booth with a banner and chalkboard sign" /></figure>
      <Video name="releaf-booth" label="Walkthrough of the ReLeaf trade show booth" caption="Booth walkthrough." />
    </div>
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><b>Finalist</b><span>Skandalaris Venture Competition at WashU, as a freshman</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>Winner</b><span>IdeaBounce, through live pitching</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>Official</b><span>Now a real company, with a pilot program planned in California</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="journey">
      <Video name="releaf-journey" label="Highlight reel of the ReLeaf journey: trade shows, pitching on stage, and awards" caption="The journey so far: trade shows, pitches, and a few awards along the way." />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="learned" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="What I learned">What I learned</h2>
    <p>
      ReLeaf taught me how a business actually runs. <strong>Customer discovery</strong> taught me to listen closely to
      pain points. <strong>Salesmanship</strong> taught me to communicate value with clarity and confidence. Most of all,
      it grew my passion for product innovation and thoughtful design, and showed me how creativity and sustainability
      can work together to make something people genuinely enjoy.
    </p>
    <p>ReLeaf Candles is the first chapter. One day, <a href="/playground/jdel">JDel</a> will be real too.</p>
  </section>
</CaseLayout>

<style>
  .palette { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 8px 0 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: 10px; }
  .palette li { aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 14px; background: var(--sw); display: flex; align-items: flex-end; padding: 8px; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08); }
  .palette span { font-size: 0.72rem; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 6px; }
  .journey { max-width: 520px; margin-top: 20px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .palette { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
</style>
